    {
      "id": "agent-one-text-447",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 64,
      "y": 11070.62,
      "width": 1432,
      "height": 330.62,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1592508399,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1839349622,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794860000000,
      "created": 1794860000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "section": "agent-one"
      },
      "text": "sentence 360439  ·  status rejected  ·  reason no_credible_source\nLtd (‘HEPL’) entered into a contract with the Union of India in November, 1996 in relation\nto the extraction, development and production of hydrocarbons in a geographic block in India\n(“Block”).\n\nwhy it cannot be resolved\n  1  the sentence starts at \"Ltd\": the rest of the company name\n     sits in the sentence before it, so this string alone cannot\n     name the company\n  2  \"HEPL\" is a short form and this sentence never spells it\n     out, so there is nothing here to match a full name against\n  3  resolve_mention(\"HEPL\", this sentence) -> candidates: []\n     nothing reached the 0.700 credibility line\n  4  SPRING reads the company as a name with one op, \"Ltd.\",\n     which is the same cut-off, seen from the graph side\n  5  with no name to write, the agent writes no graph and no\n     rewrite, and the sentence is marked rejected\n\nwhat is kept\n  rejected.jsonl  { sentence_id 360439, original, status rejected,\n                    reason no_credible_source, candidates [] }\n  5 of the 6 sentences of this article were accepted; this one is\n  data too, kept with its reason for a person to review",
      "fontSize": 11.5,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "sentence 360439  ·  status rejected  ·  reason no_credible_source\nLtd (‘HEPL’) entered into a contract with the Union of India in November, 1996 in relation\nto the extraction, development and production of hydrocarbons in a geographic block in India\n(“Block”).\n\nwhy it cannot be resolved\n  1  the sentence starts at \"Ltd\": the rest of the company name\n     sits in the sentence before it, so this string alone cannot\n     name the company\n  2  \"HEPL\" is a short form and this sentence never spells it\n     out, so there is nothing here to match a full name against\n  3  resolve_mention(\"HEPL\", this sentence) -> candidates: []\n     nothing reached the 0.700 credibility line\n  4  SPRING reads the company as a name with one op, \"Ltd.\",\n     which is the same cut-off, seen from the graph side\n  5  with no name to write, the agent writes no graph and no\n     rewrite, and the sentence is marked rejected\n\nwhat is kept\n  rejected.jsonl  { sentence_id 360439, original, status rejected,\n                    reason no_credible_source, candidates [] }\n  5 of the 6 sentences of this article were accepted; this one is\n  data too, kept with its reason for a person to review",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
